        <div style="margin-left:20pt; margin-top:17.5pt; width:436pt; line-height:12pt;font-weight:bold;">
          <font style="letter-spacing:-0.2pt;">Liquidity and Capital Resources</font><font style="font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:0.2pt;"> </font>
        </div>
        <div style="text-indent:20pt; margin-top:8pt; width:456pt; line-height:12.5pt;">
          <font style="letter-spacing:0.2pt;">Kestrel finances its operations through a combination of contributed equity and cash generated internally from operations. Kestrel believes that there will be access to debt capital in the near future as its business continues to scale. Kestrel will continue to evaluate all capital sources available to it in order to efficiently fund Kestrel&#8217;s anticipated growth. Kestrel currently has no debt outstanding. </font>
        </div>
        <div style="text-indent:20pt; margin-top:8pt; width:456pt; line-height:12.5pt;">
          <font style="letter-spacing:0.2pt;">Kestrel considers all liquid investments with original maturities of three&#160;months or less to be cash equivalents. Kestrel does not consider uninvested cash held in investment accounts as cash or cash equivalents. As of December&#160;31, 2024 and 2023, cash equivalents consisted primarily of money market accounts. </font>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div style="margin-top:2.00000000000002pt;height:12pt;margin-left:69.66pt;width:456pt;">
        <div style="margin-top:5pt; text-align:center; width:456pt; line-height:12pt;">
          <font style="letter-spacing:0.2pt;">&#160;</font>
